      "input": "# How Packet Switching Scales\n\n在分组交换网络里，延迟不是固定值，而是分布。Engineers model queue depth with λ and μ, then reason about tail latency p95 / p99.\nThis fixture intentionally mixes English and 中文，包含 emoji 🧪、希腊字母 α β γ、以及重音词汇 naive, façade, café.\n\n## Observations\n\n> A network is a conversation between clocks.\n> 当时钟漂移累积时，重传策略会放大 jitter，而不是“修复”它。\n\n1. Measure first: collect RTT, loss ratio, and reorder depth.\n2. Stabilize second: tune timeout, backoff, and retry budget.\n3. Review continuously: compare weekly medians and tail percentiles.\n\n- [x] telemetry pipeline emits structured traces\n- [ ] anomaly detector still needs threshold tuning\n\n| metric | baseline | stressed |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: |\n| p50 latency (ms) | 12.4 | 18.9 |\n| p99 latency (ms) | 44.0 | 131.6 |\n| loss rate (%) | 0.03 | 0.42 |\n\n```ts\nexport function classify(delayMs: number): string {\n  if (delayMs < 20) return 'fast'\n  if (delayMs < 80) return 'steady'\n  return 'tail'\n}\n```\n\nWhen traffic surges, the parser should still preserve inline tokens like `code`, **strong**, *emphasis*, ~~delete~~,\nand links such as <https://example.com/spec> or [queueing note][q-note].\n\n$$\nL = λ × W\n$$\n\n[q-note]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queueing_theory \"Queueing Theory\"\n",
